      "title": "Firefox Smart Window adds tab-aware AI form filling",
      "summary": "Mozilla updated Smart Window in Firefox to monitor open browser tabs and automatically populate online forms, such as transferring LinkedIn career data directly into multi-field job applications.",
      "key_facts": [
        "Monitors open tabs to auto-populate forms",
        "Requires at least four text fields to trigger"
      ],
      "design_implication": "A user hitting a multi-step checkout or application form no longer types across isolated fields. With the browser synthesizing unstructured background context into inputs, validation shifts from per-field typing errors to high-level review of pre-filled values. Audit form architectures to expose confirmation states and field sources so users can verify imported context before submission.",
